#X obj 60 678 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 706 1 float: note number. Velocity is taken from inlet 2 \;   and velocity 0 is a note off. \; 1 list: note and velocity. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages. \; 2 float: velocity for the next note \, 0 to 127 (default 100). \; 3 anything: a message \, the same set as inlet 1., f 64;
#X obj 60 816 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 844 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: preset names and state \, as name and value., f 64;
#X obj 60 906 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 934 preset n: select a patch and report its name. \; presets: report every patch as preset \, number \, name \, \;   then presets and the count. \; info: report the current state \, one message per value. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bendrange. \; mod f: modulation lever \, 0 to 1. \; aftertouch f: channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; stop: all notes off. \; reset: all notes off and the effect tails emptied., f 64;
#X obj 60 1108 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1136 notein: note and velocity as a list into inlet 1. \; bendin: scaled to -1..1 and sent as bend. \; ctlin 1: modulation lever \, sent as mod. \; ctlin 64: hold pedal \, sent as sustain. \; touchin: channel pressure \, sent as aftertouch. \; pgmin: program change \, minus 1 \, sent as preset., f 64;
#X obj 60 1246 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1274 preset (0): patch number \, counted from 0 over all loaded banks. \; volume (80): master volume in percent. \; reverb (patch): reverb balance \, dry to wet. \; chorus (patch): chorus balance \, dry to wet. \; balance (patch): tone balance \, lower tone at 0 \, upper tone at 100. Without effect on patches that use one tone. \; tune (0): master tune in cents. \; voices (8): polyphony per tone. A patch that uses one tone plays twice as many notes. \; bendrange (patch): range of the bend message in semitones., f 64;
#X obj 60 1464 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1492 The object contains no Roland data. It loads two kinds of file from the folder of the external \, or else from the folder of the patch. \; d50_pcm.bin: the PCM samples \, written by tools/make_d50_data.py from your own ROM images. Without it the object stays silent and says so in the Pd window. \; Every .syx file beside it is read as a D-50 bulk dump of 64 patches. The files are loaded in alphabetical order \, PND50-00.syx first \, and their patches are numbered through. Without a bank the object plays eight built-in presets. \; The engine runs at 32 kHz \, the rate of the original \, and is resampled to the rate of Pd., f 64;
#X obj 60 1698 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X floatatom 60 1726 4 0 127 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 1750 preset \$1;
#X obj 60 1776 s \$0-d50;
#X obj 190 1726 r \$0-d50-out;
#X obj 190 1750 route preset;
#X obj 190 1776 unpack f s;
#X floatatom 190 1804 4 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X symbolatom 250 1804 22 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 82 1832 The patches live in the object. Send preset n to select one. The third outlet answers with the number and the name \, which is all a panel or a headless host needs. \; A patch change resets reverb \, chorus \, equalizer \, balance \, bendrange and portamento to the values stored in the patch., f 64;
#X obj 60 1926 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Performance 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 1978 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 1954 6 -1 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 1978 bend \$1;
#X floatatom 160 1954 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 1978 mod \$1;
#X floatatom 260 1954 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 260 1978 aftertouch \$1;
#X floatatom 360 1954 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 360 1978 sustain \$1;
#X text 82 2008 bend (0): pitch wheel \, -1 to 1. The range in semitones is bendrange. \; mod (0): modulation lever \, 0 to 1. What it does is part of the patch. \; aftertouch (0): channel pressure \, 0 to 1. \; sustain (0): hold pedal. Notes released while it is 1 sound until it returns to 0., f 64;
#X obj 460 2148 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2124 6 0 1 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2148 porta \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2124 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2148 portatime \$1;
#X text 82 2178 porta (patch): portamento switch. \; portatime (patch): portamento time \, 0 to 100., f 64;
#X obj 60 2224 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Reverb 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 2276 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2252 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2276 reverb \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2252 6 1 32 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2276 reverbtype \$1;
#X text 82 2306 reverb (patch): reverb balance \, 0 is dry. \; reverbtype (patch): one of the 32 rooms \, halls \, delays and gates of the D-50. A change of type empties the reverb., f 64;
#X obj 60 2368 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Chorus 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2396 The D-50 has one chorus per tone. These messages set both tones together., f 64;
#X obj 460 2456 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2432 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2456 chorus \$1;
#X floatatom 160 2432 6 1 8 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 160 2456 chorustype \$1;
#X text 82 2486 chorus (patch): chorus balance \, 0 is dry. \; chorustype (patch): chorus 1 and 2 \, flanger 1 and 2 \, feedback chorus \, tremolo \, chorus tremolo \, dimension., f 64;
#X obj 460 2562 s \$0-d50;
#X floatatom 60 2538 6 0 100 0 - - - 0;
#X msg 60 2562 chorusrate \$1;
